# Recorded from real T5AI hardware on 2026-09-01.
# Device: CH342 dual-port USB-serial (1a86:55d2), port A, serial 5AAE168564.
# Command: tyutool_cli write -d t5ai -p COM34 -s 0x0 -f <16 KiB>
#   -> reset, handshake, flash id, unprotect, 4x sector erase, write,
#      per-sector CRC verify, protect, reboot. 921600 baud.
#
# Safe to take on real hardware, for two reasons checked before recording:
#  1. 16 KiB never triggers the 64 KiB block erase (ops.rs use_block_erase
#     needs remaining >= 64 KiB), so the erased range equals the written one.
#  2. The bytes written are the device head it already held -- the first
#     16 KiB of the public auth-firmware-t5ai-1.1.1.bin. Reads before and
#     after both matched it, so flash content is unchanged by this recording,
#     and the fixture carries nothing the device kept private.
#
# A recording of an authorize run may never be committed: that traffic is
# credentials in plaintext.
#
# Do not hand-edit. If the protocol changes on purpose, re-record on hardware.
#
